{"summary":"Verified a current, source-backed faculty-fit shortlist for Priya’s single-cell host–pathogen interests and separately checked EMBL’s official recruiting-group list. Scientific fit is supported for three current EMBL group leaders; current student acceptance is verified only at the programme-list level, and none of the three appears on the current recruiting list.","sections":[{"title":"Shortlist","body":"1. Wolfgang Huber — strongest computational/single-cell fit. EMBL identifies him as Group Leader and Senior Scientist in Heidelberg. His group develops statistical and computational methods for single-cell and spatial omics, CRISPR/drug perturbation assays, quantitative imaging, and biomedical/clinical datasets. This directly matches Priya’s scRNA-seq, R/Python, Bayesian-modelling, and malaria-related profile. citeturn0search4turn0search9

2. Nassos Typas — strongest bacterial host–pathogen/microbial-systems fit. EMBL identifies him as Head of Molecular Systems Biology and Group Leader. His group studies bacterial cellular networks, sequencing-enabled genome-wide readouts, antibiotic resistance, and pathogenic or commensal bacteria in microbiomes. An official EMBL project description hosted by Typas specifically involves pathogenic/commensal E. coli, sequencing pipelines, metagenomics, Python/R, and machine learning. citeturn0search1turn0search10turn0search12

3. Jordi van Gestel — credible adjacent fit. EMBL identifies him as a Heidelberg Group Leader. His group combines quantitative single-cell microscopy, functional genomics, high-content CRISPR libraries, experimental evolution, and mathematical modelling to study microbial predator–prey and emerging host–symbiont/host–pathogen interactions. The match is less direct for human infection or malaria than Huber or Typas. citeturn0search2turn0search5"},{"title":"Fit versus acceptance evidence","body":"The official EMBL International PhD Programme recruiting page says its listed groups are actively looking to hire PhD students and that the list is preliminary and may change. The current list includes the Typas Group but does not include the Huber Group or van Gestel Group. Therefore, current EIPP recruitment is verified for Typas at the programme-list level only; it is not verified for Huber or van Gestel. This does not establish that Typas has a project matching Priya’s exact interests, only that the group is currently listed as recruiting. citeturn0search0"},{"title":"Programme timing","body":"EMBL’s official application page states that 2026 Summer Recruitment is closed and that the next 2027 Winter Recruitment opens in September 2026. The page also explains that applicants select groups of interest and that both recruiting and non-recruiting Group Leaders participate in the virtual panel assessment. citeturn0search7turn0search11"},{"title":"Recommended ordering","body":"Prioritise Huber for computational single-cell and spatial-omics alignment; Typas for bacterial infection, microbiome, pathogen genomics, and current EIPP recruitment; and van Gestel as a broader microbial-interaction option. Do not state that Huber or van Gestel are accepting students. For Typas, state only that the group appears on EMBL’s current recruiting-group list, not that a specific project or supervisor slot is guaranteed."}],"drafts":[],"follow_ups":["Recheck EMBL’s recruiting-group page when the 2027 Winter Recruitment opens in September 2026.","If contacting groups later, ask whether a project involving single-cell host-response analysis or pathogen genomics is available within the relevant recruitment round."],"sources":[{"title":"EMBL International PhD Programme — Recruiting Group Leaders","url":"https://www.embl.org/about/info/embl-international-phd-programme/recruiting-group-leaders/"},{"title":"EMBL International PhD Programme — Application","url":"https://www.embl.org/about/info/embl-international-phd-programme/application/"},{"title":"EMBL Huber Group — Quantitative Biology and Statistics","url":"https://www.embl.org/groups/huber/"},{"title":"EMBL Typas Group — Systems microbiology","url":"https://www.embl.org/groups/typas/"},{"title":"EMBL van Gestel Group — Evolution of microbial life cycles","url":"https://www.embl.org/groups/van-gestel/"},{"title":"EMBL project description hosted by Nassos Typas","url":"https://www.embl.org/about/info/scientific-visitor-programme/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/EUR_Project_descriptions_Call-2025.pdf"}],"prepared_result":true,"external_change_confirmed":false,"payment_boundary_reached":false,"purchase_confirmed":false}
